Your file rendered, but the report shows it is not a true star: the outline is a circle (diameter 156.79 mm) centred on the origin, and every horizontal slice is identical. That means no points are being resolved and the shape has no angular variation. The fix is to define the star as a 2D shape in the XY plane and extrude it with `linear_extrude`, which keeps the profile constant through the thickness.

Below is the corrected file. It builds the same 8-pointed star (outer radius 30 mm, inner radius 18 mm, first outer point on +X) and punches the 8 mm centre hole.

```openscad
// Star-shaped indexing wheel
// Print orientation: flat on bed, z = 0 to plate_t

// ---------- Parameters ----------
outer_r   = 30;   // distance of outer points from centre
inner_r   = 18;   // distance of inner points from centre
point_n   = 8;    // number of points (and inner points)
plate_t   = 4;    // plate thickness
hole_d    = 8;    // central through-hole diameter
eps       = 0.5;  // cutter overshoot past faces

$fn = 96;

// ---------- Model ----------
